  "notes": [
    "Primary diagnostic is independent 12k-minus-8k bb/100 with a raw normal CI from all 10,000 hands. Call external dose reversal clear only if that CI upper bound is below zero. Downgrade the bounded-residual route if both 8k and 12k raw upper CIs are below the Standard10 point estimate. Otherwise treat point-order evidence as suggestive and prioritize multi-seed or greater precision."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "The exact 8k bundle completed eight independent fresh625 sessions (5,000 hands) at -34.42 bb/100 CI[-76.932,+8.092], with seats -26.498 and -42.368. All 15,053 decisions and 20,053 requests passed replay/evidence audits. Relative to the independent 12k fresh5k, 12k-minus-8k was -20.11 bb/100 CI[-77.190,+36.970], opposite the internal +21.758 slope but not statistically resolved. Full suite: 241 passed.",
    "conclusion": "The external point curve reverses the internally positive 8k-to-12k curve, but independent-sample uncertainty is too wide to call a clear dose reversal. The preregistered route-downgrade condition also failed because the 8k upper CI exceeds both zero and the Standard10 point. Six-objective MGDA remains a real training mechanism whose current internal evaluation is not a reliable promotion proxy.",
    "decision": "HOLD_MGDA_EXTERNAL_DOSE_DIRECTION_PENDING_MULTI_SEED",
    "next_step": "Do not expand seed0 to 20k or increase its training dose. Obtain one independent-seed external checkpoint observation, preferably seed1 12k because it already has an exact frozen checkpoint and internally different seat behavior. Use it to distinguish seed-specific variance from route-level transfer failure; then either redesign the external-aligned training objective or resume geometric scaling only with a validated proxy."
  },
